The '''Tree Gnome Village Dungeon''' is found beneath the [[Tree Gnome Village (location)|Tree Gnome Village]]. Its surface entrance is in the maze just south of the main village area.

The dungeon features in [[Waterfall Quest]], where players visit it to obtain [[glarial's pebble]] from [[Golrie]]. To reach Golrie, a [[Key (Gnome Village Dungeon)|key]] must first be obtained from the eastern room, which is inhabited by [[zombie]]s and [[giant bat]]s. The key is found in the large [[Crate (Tree Gnome Village Dungeon)|crate]] in the south-east corner that is coloured differently from the rest of the crates. The key can then be used in the western room full of [[hobgoblin]]s to unlock the door Golrie is imprisoned behind.

After starting [[Roving Elves]], Golrie and the hobgoblins swap positions, and the key to the now-imprisoned hobgoblins can instead be obtained by simply speaking to Golrie.

During [[The Path of Glouphrie]], the player gains access to a storeroom in the east of the dungeon, containing a [[singing bowl]] as well as [[Yewnock]]'s anti-illusion machine.

